<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Ponce de León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1474–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Ponce de León was a Spanish conquistador who began the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a> in 1508 and became its first governor. In 1513 he led the first known European expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> and gave it its name. He returned in 1521 to found a colony but was wounded in a fight with the Calusa and died soon after in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-ponce-de-leon.jpg" alt="Juan Ponce de León" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Ponce_de_Le%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
